Integer coefficients for the element routines in this addon.


Procedure pointers
------------------

Summary of assignment of user functions/subroutines to procedure pointers:

  coefficients%func1(1)%p => etafunc     ! scalar function for the viscosity
                                         ! in generalized stokes elements
  coefficients%func1(2)%p => eta0func    ! scalar function for the
                                         ! zero-shear-rate viscosity
  coefficients%func1(3)%p => etainffunc  ! scalar function for the
                                         ! infinite-shear-rate viscosity
  coefficients%func1(4)%p => lambdafunc  ! scalar function for the
                                         ! time scale in the viscosity
  coefficients%func1(5)%p => eta_const   ! scalar function for the
                                         ! constant viscosity for gnmodel=0
  coefficients%func1(6)%p => tauyfunc    ! scalar function for the
                                         ! yield stress

NOTES:

 1) The user functions/subroutines only need to be assigned if they are
    actually being used. If a required assignment is forgotten an error message
    with be given.
 2) The user is free to choose the functions/subroutines for assignment as
    long as the interface is correct.


List of the coefficients
------------------------

  1-150: all relevant integer coefficients for the stokes & viscoelastic add-on
151-200: reserved for diffuse_interface add-on
201-250: reserved for inertia add-on


251  The viscosity coefficient eta is as follows:
       0: constant, given by coefficients%r(1)
       1: given by a function, funcnr=coefficient%i(252)
          NOTE: scalar function must be assigned to coefficients%func1(1)%p
       2: given by nodal values in the vector oldvectors%v(1)
       3: given by the vector per element oldvectors%e(1)

     NOTE if coefficients%i(251)==3:
       * the elvector for the matrix/vector is in the Gauss points
       * the elvector for the postprocessing is in the nodal points
     see also coefficients%i(255).

     NOTE: The viscosity coefficient eta is used to obtain a space and/or
       time dependent viscosity in the generalized_stokes elements.
       In the generalized_newtonian elements it is not used.

252  funcnr for the viscosity coefficient eta.

253  Iteration scheme used in generalized_newtonian_elements:
     0: Picard. Note: (u,p) is the solution vector.
     1: Newton-Raphson. Note: (delta u,p) is the solution vector.

254  gnmodel: viscosity function for the generalized Newtonian model
     (gd=shearrate):
       0: Constant, i.e. not dependent on gd.
            eta = eta_const
       1: Power law
            eta = m * (gd)^(n-1)
       2: Carreau
            eta = eta_inf + (eta_0 - eta_inf) / (1 + (lambda*gd)^2)^{(1-n)/2}
       3: Carreau-Yasuda
            eta = eta_inf + (eta_0 - eta_inf) / (1 + (lambda*gd)^a)^{(1-n)/a}

255  Compute the viscosity (to be stored in elvector) in the
       0: Gauss points
       1: nodal points
     Options 0 is for computing the element matrix/vector and options 1 is for
     postprocessing (such as stress).

256  Random number generator for the stochastic term:
       1: create random vectors with uniform distribution
          uses the fortran intrinsic function random_number
       2: create random vectors with uniform distribution
          uses the ziggurat random_number generator
       3: create random vectors with normal distribution
          uses the ziggurat random_number generator

