     NOTE: The viscosity coefficient eta_const is used to obtain a space and/or
       time dependent viscosity in the generalized newtonian elements.
       Together with a yield model it is possible to define a Bingham model.

264  funcnr for the viscosity coefficient eta_const.

265  yieldmodel: yield function for the viscosity of the generalized
     Newtonian model (gd=shearrate):
       0: No yield function
       1: Bingham, i.e. constant yield stress
            eta = tau_y / gd
       2: Regularized Bingham (Papanastasiou)
            eta = tau_y ( 1 - exp(-r*gd) ) / gd

     NOTE: The viscosity of the fluid is given by sum of the viscosity
     function given by gnmodel (coefficients%i(254)) and the yield model.

     NOTE: The Bingham model (yieldmodel=1) does not show convergence in the
     current viscosity implementation. Do not use this model! Other methods
     are required, but these are currently not available in tfem.

